{
    "name": "John Clopton",
    "birthDate": "1756-02-07",
    "deathDate": "1816-09-11",
    "bio": "a Representative from Virginia; born in St. Peter's parish, near Tunstall, New Kent County, Va., February 7, 1756; graduated from the College of Philadelphia (now the University of Pennsylvania) in 1776; studied law; admitted to the bar and practiced; served in the Revolutionary War as first lieutenant and as captain; wounded at the Battle of Brandywine; member of the Virginia state house of delegates, 1789-1791; elected as a Democratic Republican to the Fourth and to the succeeding Congress (March 4, 1795-March 3, 1799); member of the Virginia privy council, 1799-1801; elected to the Seventh and to the seven succeeding Congresses and served from March 4, 1801, until his death near Tunstall, Va., September 11, 1816; chairman, Committee on Revisal and Unfinished Business (Tenth Congress); interment in the family burying ground on his plantation.",
